{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>ויקחו לי תרומה.</b> לִי — for My Name." "<b>תרומה.</b> A separation — they shall separate for Me from their property a free-will offering." "<b>ידבנו לבו.</b> A term of free-will offering, and it is a term of good will; פיישנ״ט בְּלַעַז." "<b>תקחו את תרומתי.</b> Our Rabbis said: three offerings are spoken of here. One — the offering of a bekha per head, from which the sockets were made, as is explained in אֵלֶּה פְקוּדֵי. And one — the offering for the altar, a bekha per head, for the collection-boxes, to purchase from them the public offerings. And one — the offering of the Tabernacle, the free-will donation of each and every one (Talmud Yerushalmi, Shekalim 1). Thirteen things are spoken of in the matter — all of them were needed for the work of the Tabernacle or for the garments of the priesthood, as you examine them closely."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {2 "the la'az is Old French pesant, 'willing/pleased'"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:54:22.179756656Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}